{"name":"Cherry Paddle Pop","hex":"#fe314b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cherry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small fruit, usually red, black or yellow, with a smooth hard seed and a short hard stem.","Prunus subg. Cerasus, trees or shrubs that bear cherries."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the taste of cherries.","Of a bright red color; cherry red."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cherry"},{"term":"paddle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A two-handed implement consisting of a shaft with one or two blades attached to the end(s) used to propel a canoe, kayak or a small boat. A paddle is unattached to the boat and freely operated with the hands, compared with an oar which is attached to the boat at a pivot point.\nA single-bladed version is typically used on canoes and some other small boats.\nA double-bladed version with blades at each end of the shaft is used for kayaking.","A single-bladed version is typically used on canoes and some other small boats."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To propel something through water with a paddle, oar, hands, etc.","To row a boat with less than one's full capacity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paddle"},{"term":"pop","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Pwapwâ."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A loud, sharp sound, as of a cork coming out of a bottle, especially when the contents are pressurized by fizziness.","An effervescent or fizzy drink, most frequently nonalcoholic; soda pop."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pop"}],"entries":[{"title":"Paddle Pop","blocks":[{"text":"Paddle Pop  is a brand of ice confection products originally created by Streets, which is owned by The Magnum Ice Cream Company. It is sold in Australia, New Zealand, and a few other countries. It is held for eating by a wooden stick which protrudes at the base. The brand has a mascot known as the Paddle Pop Lion, or Max, who appears on the product wrapper."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paddle_Pop"},{"title":"Cherry","blocks":[{"text":"A cherry is the fruit of many plants of the genus Prunus, and is a fleshy drupe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg/330px-Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry"},{"title":"Paddle","blocks":[{"text":"A paddle is a handheld tool with an elongated handle and a flat, widened end used as a lever to apply force onto the bladed end. It most commonly describes a completely handheld tool used to propel a human-powered watercraft by pushing water in a direction opposite to the direction of travel. A paddle is different from an oar – an oar is attached to the watercraft via a fulcrum."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/52/Raft_paddle.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paddle"},{"title":"Cerise (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Cerise is a dark pink shade."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Bandyball1.jpg/330px-Bandyball1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cerise_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Streets_Paddle_Pop_Lion_%286219677927%29.jpg/500px-Streets_Paddle_Pop_Lion_%286219677927%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Streets_Paddle_Pop_Lion_%286219677927%29.jpg/500px-Streets_Paddle_Pop_Lion_%286219677927%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Paddle Pop Lion mascot costume","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File